    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vinnie Pasquantino** leads the charge with a 72.66 score, benefiting from an advantageous matchup against Morris (xERA 4.14) and a favorable right-handed platoon boost that pushes him into \"Strong\" territory. Close behind, **Brice Turang** (68.93) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.97) are must-starts. **Brice Turang** earns his high marks by facing Houser\u2019s porous 4.75 xERA, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority play despite a lefty-on-lefty matchup; his sprint speed and the high SB probability against Wrobleski\u2019s slow delivery outweigh the platoon regression. **Henry Bolte** (60.92) is our tactical surprise, vaulting into \"Strong\" status thanks to favorable wind conditions and a leadoff spot that maximizes his plate appearance volume against Imanaga.\n\nThe decision to start **Jose Caballero** (55.07) over other options was driven almost entirely by the pursuit of stolen bases, as he offers the best late-lineup upside against Cecconi. The tightest margin on the board involved **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose 57.81 score barely squeezed him ahead of our deeper bench assets. While **Tyler Soderstrom** carries some risk against the crafty Imanaga, his power profile keeps him in the mix. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, whose scores are currently tempered by \"Lineup Pending\" status; if either is pushed lower than their assumed batting order, their floor-level scores of 54.71 and 50.74, respectively, could collapse further, necessitating a late swap if we weren't already thin at those positions. \n\nOur bench remains stagnant today due to the scheduled off-days for **Josh Naylor** and **James Wood**, while **Mickey Moniak** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our late-game contingency options. The remainder of our organizational depth, including **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Kyle Karros**, **Cole Young**, and **Carson Williams**, are currently rostered for long-term depth or recovery and were not considered for today's starting rotation. We proceed with today's lineup knowing that **Austin Riley** (42.73) represents the weakest link in our daily efficiency chain, as he battles the elite pitch-mix of Fluharty.",
